{"id": "EUVD-2026-86815", "enisaUuid": "a6e02639-62cc-3541-9e4a-f20575933880", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nperf/core: Allow list_del during perf_event_overflow()\n\nA PMU might use perf_sched_cb_inc() and perf_sched_cb_dec()\ninterface to get the PMU call back function pmu::sched_task\ninvoked at schedule in and schedule out. This is achieved\nby walking along the list anchored by sched_cb_list.\n\nThe following scenario might lead to a list corruption.\n\n   perf_pmu_sched_task()\n      for_each_list_entry(..., &sched_cb_list)\n      +--> __perf_pmu_sched_task()\n           +--> event->pmu->sched_task())\n                +--> PMU_push_sample()\n                     +--> perf_event_overflow()\n                          +--> __perf_event_overflow()\n                               +--> pmu->stop()\n                                    +--> perf_sched_cb_dec()\n                                         remove entry from sched_cb_list\n                                         while list node in use.\n\nThis happens when ioctl(fd, PERF_EVENT_IOC_REFRESH, xxx) has been\ninvoked and perf_event::event_limit hits zero.\n\nPrevent the list corruption and convert for_each_list_entry()\nto for_each_list_entry_safe().", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fa360a018369f3eb4fe4f4792238adfc1f6fd5dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/723e85fb2c3bcd237ac02cbd69502ed62ce0068c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d0b9ce3be221c9077653f3670d60d66bb725ee2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2770c76a02452fddb52e9e05c7ed6acfef06c32", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/59e63416f5153e7d58652c616fbdcb7d5e01fff7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97961", "GHSA-prpp-c3xm-jcfh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b927b1f-6f08-37ef-8ebd-ac6a42985df3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2ec38fab-3e04-3b87-8d64-eac656749906", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <6d0b9ce3be221c9077653f3670d60d66bb725ee2"}, {"id": "30ea87ed-4c22-3401-8117-94d437b30f8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <59e63416f5153e7d58652c616fbdcb7d5e01fff7"}, {"id": "38674107-a6be-3a0b-aea7-6a35ba0d0a01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <e2770c76a02452fddb52e9e05c7ed6acfef06c32"}, {"id": "500a80a8-4448-320d-a31d-f2e42c487141", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "6a42e973-8c23-34c5-a8bd-85ddb9aad771", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "885a865a-10f9-33be-9da0-a3e27c648085", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <fa360a018369f3eb4fe4f4792238adfc1f6fd5dc"}, {"id": "987367f2-2f12-3345-bfce-a0188ce4a73f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "c9921d02-b648-3e2f-840a-b111771a6e83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "d89c809f-565e-33f9-aa33-5ed76ebcf81b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e635d975-e8c7-3b53-9b2b-5c277bdd1e6c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd27568117664b8b3e259721393df420ed51f57b <723e85fb2c3bcd237ac02cbd69502ed62ce0068c"}, {"id": "f1284917-a967-3040-a6c8-2468f0f5016a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fe6ff463-1578-3597-8a6d-0d7fffc9c291", "ven